	 <note id="GUID-0C2E7F90-C696-4E9F-A9FC-4576C7EA156C"> 
		<p> Preliminary values and subject to change 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>1</sup> NVL and PTL DF, Ψ<sub>si</sub>, Ψ<sub>sn -hp</sub> , and Ψ<sub>hp-a</sub> are calculated using Intel Technology Targets based on most up to date test data. 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>2</sup> DF<sub>Thermal_Solution</sub> is different from the Global DF, check 
		  <xref scope="local" format="dita" href="GUID-1D89D292-7CD3-4E06-9D28-4E18877EC4E0.dita"><?xm-replace_text Calculating Mobile Cooling Needs at Target PL1 (1)?></xref> for definition. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>3</sup> DF<sub>Thermal_Solution</sub> is sensitive to the nature of the workload, Ψ<sub>sn-hp</sub> and Ψ<sub>hp-a</sub> are less sensitive to the nature of workload. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>4</sup> The transient performance for the first 5-10s is largely insensitive to Ψ<sub>hp-a</sub> and the heat exchanger should be sized for sustained PL1. Refer 
		  <xref scope="local" format="dita" href="GUID-C502FA2A-FDE3-45D8-ABFE-FDE87310920A.dita"><?xm-replace_text Transient Heat Pipe Guidance - Design for PL2 (1)?></xref> for details on the RPM effect on the temperature increase and additional design guidance for improved transient performance. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>5</sup> The thermal solution used is 1.3mm cold plate soldered to 3 heat pipes (2nos. of original diameter of 6mm crushed to 1.6mm, 1no. of original diameter of 8mm crushed to 1.6mm) 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>6</sup>The thermal solution used is 3mm cold plate soldered to 2 heat pipes (1no. of original diameter of 8mm crushed to 2mm, 1no. of original diameter of 10mm crushed to 2mm) 
		</p> 
	 </note> 
